<title>BRAZIL: Brazil's Vale signs accord with Hyundai.</title>
<headline>Brazil's Vale signs accord with Hyundai.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazilian mining giant Companhia Vale do Rio Doce on Tuesday signed a cooperation accord with South Korean industrial conglomerate Hyundai Corp, the private Invest News agency reported.</p>
<p>The agency said the accord could pave the way for $500 million in South Korean direct foreign investment in Brazil to boost exports of minerals, aluminium, paper and timber.</p>
<p>The agreement came during a visit to Brazil by South Korean President Kim Young-sam.</p>
<p>Vale is due to be privatized next year.</p>
<p>-- Michael Christie, Brasilia newsroom 55-61-2230358</p>
